{
  "_readme": [
    "The CROSS-PIN. Every case here is asserted twice: against the browser's own",
    "mapping in ui.js / svg.js / structure.js / core/state.js (render_crosspin.test.mjs)",
    "and against the Python port in zicato/tui/present.py (tests/test_tui_crosspin.py).",
    "",
    "The two surfaces render the same served model, so they must agree about what",
    "'stalled' means, when a rating is provisional, whether an absent outcome is a",
    "rejection, and — the one with teeth at runtime — whether a state_change frame",
    "is worth any work at all. Changing either implementation without changing the",
    "other fails here: this file is the contract, not documentation."
  ],
